Interruption, restoration and the evidence for returning service (@wu-restoration: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #source "../sources/Water-Safety-Plan-Manual-WHO.lingua#r_3JMZKS3FG80FKX9YRQPEJMA4VD", #source "../sources/Sanitation-Safety-Planning-WHO.lingua#r_2FF0R519TGR5RNY3EVV7APPZ86", #source "../sources/Operational-Technology-Security-NIST.lingua#r_4W20M55VVPGFB1FAB00Q347KPT", #water-and-sanitation "The-people-materials-and-finance-that-keep-water-working.lingua#r_2ZW9VV6JHPB69ZRZ9FC0AKHNXX") { r_3XQQ1GBTMB02T47TT6PEG457CD
**Read:** [Water safety plan manual — WHO and IWA, second edition](../sources/Water-Safety-Plan-Manual-WHO.lingua#r_3JMZKS3FG80FKX9YRQPEJMA4VD), management and incident response; [Sanitation safety planning — WHO, second edition](../sources/Sanitation-Safety-Planning-WHO.lingua#r_2FF0R519TGR5RNY3EVV7APPZ86), affected sanitation pathways; [Operational technology security — NIST SP 800-82, revision 3](../sources/Operational-Technology-Security-NIST.lingua#r_4W20M55VVPGFB1FAB00Q347KPT), recovery; revisit the distribution repair and restart material.

Restoration is a sequence of physical and informational changes. Power may return before a source, treatment barrier, measurement or receiving route becomes available. Restart can mobilize deposits, change flows, expose stale water and resume a process whose stored state no longer describes reality.

**Work:** Conduct a tabletop reconstruction of a fictional outage: what is known at each time, who can act, what is isolated, which users lose service, what substitute is actually available and which observations support each return. Include a failed instrument and a delayed repair delivery. Explain residuals and diverted water as well as the supply endpoint.

Compare two restoration sequences against continuity and quality evidence, not merely the shortest equipment restart time. For deeper work, reconstruct a published incident using its primary timeline and distinguish established events from hypotheses. A tabletop identifies unanswered questions; restoration of a real health-related service requires its competent operating and public-health decisions.

**Return:** [Water, sanitation and industrial utilities](../Water-sanitation-and-industrial-utilities.lingua#r_7B9GRCJFHVBEEQEXKWCR2QMMPN).
**Continue:** [The people, materials and finance that keep water working](The-people-materials-and-finance-that-keep-water-working.lingua#r_2ZW9VV6JHPB69ZRZ9FC0AKHNXX).

